1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,190
The Moon is physically shrinking, and it is triggering massive quakes.

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:08,620
Over millions of years, its molten core has cooled down.

3
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:13,350
This cooling forces the lunar crust to wrinkle like a drying raisin.

4
00:00:13,990 --> 00:00:17,400
Pause the video—can you spot where the surface just snapped?

5
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:22,650
That tiny ridge just triggered a violent moonquake lasting six full hours.

6
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:27,670
Unlike Earth quakes, there is no liquid water to absorb seismic energy.

7
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:32,670
NASA's future Artemis base sits right inside these active fault zones.

8
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:37,000
A single major quake could collapse our entire habitat in seconds.

9
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,490
And it all happens because...
